WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.848
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:07.400
This problem was part of a written interview test for Amazon in India.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:13.680
A drawer contains twelve identical black socks and twelve identical white socks.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.160
If you pick two socks at random: what is the probability of getting a matching pair?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.840
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.160
Many people think when you pick two socks they will either match or they will not match.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:46.240
Since the number of black and white socks are equal, the probability of matching should be 50%.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:54.640
But this tempting answer is wrong! The probability of making a pair is actually slightly less than 50%.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.940
Let's calculate and figure out why?

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.020
There are 12 white socks and 12 black socks.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.060
By symmetry

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:12.060
the probability of picking a black pair of socks equals the probability of picking a white pair of socks.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.860
So let's calculate the probability of picking a black pair of socks.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.060
There is a 12 over 24 chance the first sock is black.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.880
This is because there are 12 black socks out of 24 socks total.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.520
12 over 24 simplifies to be 1/2.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.680
Now what's the chance of picking a black sock on the second draw?

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.900
For the second sock the chance will be 11 out of 23,

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:52.540
because there are 11 black socks remaining out of a total of 23 socks remaining.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.840
The asymmetry is because we are sampling without replacement.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.240
So what does this all mean?

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:13.320
It means, the probability of picking a black pair is 1/2 times 11 over 23.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.880
This will also be the probability of picking a white pair by symmetry.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.180
So, we can put this all together to get the odds of picking a pair of matching socks.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:34.660
The probability of picking a matching pair will equal the probability of picking a black pair plus the probability of picking a white pair.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.600
Each of these is equal to 1/2 times 11 over 23.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:49.700
And therefore the probability of picking a pair of matching socks will be 11 over 23, which is approximately 47.8%.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.980
This is slightly less than 1/2.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.540
Did you figure it out?

